# Description
Fixes #624

### Root Cause
When sharing a document from an external application to Paperless Mobile, both `ReceiveSharingIntent.getInitialMedia()` (cold start) and `ReceiveSharingIntent.getMediaStream()` (stream listener) emitted the same intent. Furthermore, when the Android Activity resumed from background, Android re-emitted cached intent extras because `ReceiveSharingIntent.reset()` was never invoked, causing incoming files to be processed and uploaded multiple times.

### Solution
- Added an in-memory tracking set `_processedFilePaths` with a 10-second cooldown in `EventListenerShell` to deduplicate incoming file paths.
- Called `ReceiveSharingIntent.instance.reset()` immediately upon receiving shared media files to clear Android's cached intent extras.
- Added unit tests in `test/src/features/sharing/share_deduplication_test.dart` verifying proper deduplication of rapid share events.

